PATCH 575: the debrief as the original shows it -- the mission-over phase machine, the MGA palette
fades and the driver's per-tick DAC service, the LOADGAME hand-off, and the text/surface contexts.

board:0017.  After 574 the DEFEAT verdict reached e4bb and the debrief phases ran 0..5, yet the frame
stayed black; the oracle's frame-by-frame capture (tools/oracle/census_debrief.sh, frames 16/17) shows
what should be there: the WLOSE picture dimmed to ~53 %, "MISSION LOST" + the battle statistics typed
one glyph per tick in white, "PRESS ANY KEY TO PROCEED...", then a static wait for a key.  Getting there
took the corrections below, each verified against the engine/driver asm and, where the CPU is involved,
the instrumented DOSBox (FIST_EXCLOG, a new hook).

A. The debrief phase machine (fist.c, 0f69:c4be.. = 1000:bb4e..bc86)
  e528   the class-0x36 dirty method dispatches a FAR table (DGROUP:0xf72b = 0f69:{bb4e bb58 bc39 bc58
         bc77 bc86}); Ghidra called it near -> nothing ran.
  bb58   phase 1: [0x594] (04a3, DAC black), the outcome picture (tables 0xf703/0xf70b, campaign
         0x16/0x18) through [0x560]/[0x564], be0e, `ax=1 ; dx=[0xf6d4] ; lcall [0x5b0]` (084e fade-in),
         0240(0x14), bb34 (DAC 0xff = white + [0x58c] snapshot), `ax=0x80 bx=0 cx=0xfe dx=0x3c ; lcall
         [0x5a4]` (04e6: dim indices 0..0xfe to 0x8800/0x10000 over 60 vblanks -- 04f1 is 1774-ordered
         (AX, CX, DX, BX), the first draft had bx=0x3c, cx=0: 0xff4f bytes walked past the present
         buffer), 38cc, [0xf6d6]|=0x22, [0xf76f]=3, phase++, the text pointer (0x413c or per outcome
         [0xf6fb+2*[0x6da0]]), 52d1(10,0x12)/524e(0)/530b(0xff).  Ghidra called every driver vector
         without arguments and host-deref'd both tables.
  bc12   the typewriter: one STRSEG glyph per [0x452] tick through [0x684] (19ae), CF at the NUL.
  bc39/bc58/bc77  phases 2..4 chain the three texts ("BATTLE STATISTICS" at (0x32,0x12), "PRESS ANY
         KEY" at (0xb4,0x12)) on bc12's CF; bb4e byte/word.
  [0x59c] the fade-OUT callers 3fba/40ec called [0x59c] (04cd) instead of [0x159c]; e714/e814's two
         sites passed garbage/0xf69 as AX -- the asm says 0x20 / 0x10 steps.
  DAT_2000_3a48/4d4a/4e8a/4f84/5110/51f6/b6c6  resource-descriptor FLAG BYTES ([S+2]); typed as words,
         `= bVar` zeroed the 0x0d callback-mask byte next to them -> no relocation notices -> stale
         sprite directory after MEMMGR moves.

B. The MGA palette fades (fist_mga.c)
  0478   `mov es,[0x782] ; xor di,di ; call 0483` -- the DAC snapshot into the present buffer (was a
         NULL host pointer).
  04f1/0660/0874  the 0x300-byte fade buffer is allocated through [0xe4] = 1774 (AX, CX, DX, BX ..):
         the old (0x300, 0x788, 0x1c00) put the handle offset in CX and left BX = 0 -> the buffer went
         to the handle at DGROUP:0000.  0874 no longer re-uses a stale [0x788] (patch 132): the
         driver allocates every time and 184b frees the previous node.
  05b8/0732  the two steppers 04f1/0660 register at [0x5e8] were pristine host-pointer walks: rebuilt
         1:1 (saturating accumulators, 64-entry ramps, present = ramp[snapshot], count-down/limit,
         un-register + `[0x78a]|=0x22`).  Registered in far form (driver segment in 0x5ea).
  09c6   `cmp [0x5e8],1 ; cmc` -> CF while a stepper is registered; 04cd/04e6/084e `call 9c6 ; jb`
         WAIT for it (Ghidra folded the CF to one pass, so no fade ever took time).
  0874/04f1 rate  `mov dx,1 ; div si` = 0x10000/si: for si == 1 the quotient overflows and the CPU
         raises #DE; the ENGINE's INT-0 handler 1000:5b36 skips the DIV and returns AX = 0xffff.
         Oracle (FIST_EXCLOG): EXC 0 at the driver's 0x895 -> extender 1119:00cb -> 2082:5b36 -> iret
         with ax=ffff.  So the debrief's 1-step fade-in arms the ramp saturated and settles on the
         first tick (present = loaded - 1, the driver's own quirk).  The C division gave 0: the ramp
         never rose, and the stepper ran 65535 pumps -- the black screen.

C. The driver's per-tick DAC service and the LOADGAME hand-off
  The engine's INT-8 handler 31c3 far-calls [DGROUP:0x5e4] each tick: 0b1f (guarded by the same
  [0x738] nesting byte 31c3 already bumped, so it never runs from there) or, on a machine LOADGAME
  rates >= 0x31, the unguarded 0be2 (driver init 0x13d-0x14c, WORD compares and a WORD store into the
  vector's offset -- Ghidra compared dwords and stored a dword, zeroing the segment).  The original
  runs 0be2 (RAM: [0x5e4] = 4ec3:0be2, [0x242] = 0x4934); the port had [0x242] = 0, ran the inert
  0b1f, and the shim stood in with a palette upload per pump and per in(0x3da) poll.
  0be2   rebuilt 1:1: `shr [0x786],1 ; jae` -> upload word[0x782] (768 bytes) to the DAC; with
         [0x2a8]|[0x787] == 0 walk the DAC ANIMATION list at seg [[0x3fc]] (records {size, flags,
         countdown, reload, DAC index, count, split, ptr, data}: type 1 uploads (count-split)*3 bytes
         at ptr then split*3 inline, 2..4 count*3 at ptr) and advance it (0c89); `call [0x5e8]`; the
         [0x738] bump/unbump.  Ghidra swapped every (port, value), walked everything from host 0.
  0c89   the animation advance (rotate forward/backward with split, block step with wrap and the
         0x20/0x10/0x08 end-and-chain flags, one-shot 3/4), rebuilt 1:1 in the list segment.
  ff2c   the LOADGAME script parser (0f69:089c + the 0x1000b/0x1001f helpers): DS = [0x16c4] = the
         FIST.RUN PSP (fd1b decodes it from the extender blob), the tail's last 8 chars = offset,
         segment of the script; '>' + letter selects a section (STRSEG:0x15c), an option letter reads
         one/two 4-hex-digit words into the DGROUP vars its table names (STRSEG:0x16c); ">Z" ends with
         CF=0.  Ghidra read the tail from DGROUP:0x80, walked the tables as host pointers, dropped
         every CF; fd1b now honours `jb fd59`.  The shim (native_main.c setup_dos_env) seeds the
         FIST.RUN PSP and the byte-exact oracle script (">H C4934,0034 V0056 M0805,0400 .. >M X0300,3B40
         E0400,3B40 >O D0500,0279 CADAD,0217 HFFFF .. >Z") in place of the four hand-seeded words.
  With [0x242] = 0x4934 the engine's 2144 patches its blit loops for a 386 (cs:25fb/3dff: `mov eax`/
  `shl eax,16` = the same fill replicated to dwords -- no semantic change for the C, documented here)
  (SOUNDDVR's >= 0x32 device config at 0x252 is still never reached, so nothing changes there yet).
  fist_vga.c: the stand-in is gone; in(0x3da) is the retrace-status toggle only.

D. The text and surface contexts (024f/026e and their 17 engine sites)
  `mov bx,X ; lcall [0x554]/[0x558] ; push bx .. pop bx ; lcall [..]`: the driver methods swap the
  surface ([0x724]) / text ([0x736]) context and return the PREVIOUS one in BX (`xchg ; push ax ..
  pop bx`).  Ghidra dropped BX at 22dd, 2908/290e (x3), 49b5, 4da3, 65c2 (x2), a755 and restored with
  0 or nothing, so [0x736] was 0 from the first in-mission string on and every later text -- the
  debrief's -- ran on the do-once descriptor at DGROUP:0.  g_fist_ctx_bx (shim lane) carries the
  return; 4da3's 294d/161c and 2908's 294d get their registers back too.

Left open (board:0017/0014): 29e4 (a `pop bx` tail shared by jmp) stays arg-less; 2908/290e's
[0x156a] descriptor reads are still int*-scaled.  The INT-8 rate ([0x44c] = 0x427f = one vblank on the
oracle) that decides how many 0be2 steps a [0x452] tick sees is the shim's PIT/VGA clock since
board:0026 (landed with patch 576), so the fades now take the original's vblanks.

